@* Control Panel — the placeholder shown for a navigation module that has not
   been built yet. The feature modules arrive in their own increments. *@
@page "/m/{Module}"
@layout CpShellLayout
@* cp-stub-modules (Q4, 2026-07-30) — this route used to be gated on [Authorize]
   alone while its nav item carried no RequiredPermission, so the one remaining
   stub was advertised to, and openable by, EVERY signed-in admin regardless of
   role: a GateOperator holding only Gates.Operate saw "Live sessions · Soon" in
   its menu and could open it. The "Soon" badge is a label, not a gate.

   The catch-all now exists only to serve declared stubs, and the sole declared
   stub (/m/live-sessions) stands in for a programme-read console, so the route
   carries the same permission its nav item promises. Nav and page must name the
   SAME code — CpNavigationPermissionTests pins both halves. When a stub with a
   different permission is added, this page stops being the right home for it:
   graduate it to its own route rather than widening this gate. *@
@attribute [RequirePermission(PermissionCatalog.Sessions.View)]

<PageTitle>@PageTitle · SIMF</PageTitle>

<SimfPageHeader Title="@PageTitle" />

@* §6.16 (NAV-011) — this route is a catch-all, and it used to render "Coming
   soon" for ANY slug, so a mistyped /m/ URL got a convincing page announcing a
   module that does not exist and is not coming. Only slugs CpNavigation
   declares are real; everything else is a 404. *@
@if (IsKnownModule)
{
    <div class="simf-panel">
        <h2 class="simf-panel__title">@L["Module.ComingSoon.Title"]</h2>
        <p class="simf-panel__text">@L["Module.ComingSoon.Text"]</p>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="simf-panel">
        <p class="simf-panel__text">@L["NotFound.Text"]</p>
        <p class="simf-panel__action">
            <SimfLink Href="/">@L["NotFound.Back"]</SimfLink>
        </p>
    </div>
}
